  "caveat": "Replay of DFS Upwards/System requests from 7 Oct 2026, 13 scored days. Gross settlement is what NESO would pay at the bid price if the bid were accepted and delivered (pay-as-bid assumed; a bid is assumed accepted whenever it is at or below a price NESO actually accepted that half-hour). Electricity cost uses a market index price, not any site's tariff, and excludes levies. At the assumed site value the settlement (GBP 22,875) does not cover the electricity (GBP 28,022) on its own; the site's value for the energy makes up the difference. See `sensitivity` for other values. Not a revenue claim. DFS zone IDs are not confirmed as Scotland."
